<article class="env-definition" id="0H01">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H01">Definition <span data-tag="0H01">66.18.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\mathit{Sch}_{fppf}$ be a big fppf site containing $S$, and let $\mathit{Sch}_{\acute{e}tale}$ be the corresponding big étale site (i.e., having the same underlying category). Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. The site <em>$X_{affine, {\acute{e}tale}}$</em> of $X$ is defined as follows: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
An object of $X_{affine, {\acute{e}tale}}$ is a morphism $\varphi : U \to X$ where $U \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits ((\mathit{Sch}/S)_{\acute{e}tale})$ is an affine scheme and $\varphi $ is an étale morphism, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
a morphism $(\varphi : U \to X) \to (\varphi ' : U' \to X)$ of $X_{affine, {\acute{e}tale}}$ is given by a morphism of schemes $\chi : U \to U'$ such that $\varphi = \varphi ' \circ \chi $, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
a family of morphisms $\{ \varphi _ i : (U_ i \to X) \to (U \to X)\} _{i \in I}$ of $X_{affine, {\acute{e}tale}}$ is a covering if and only if $\{ U_ i \to U\} $ is a standard étale covering, see Topologies, Definition <a href="/tag/0219" data-tag="0219">34.4.5</a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> As usual we choose a set of coverings of this type, as in Sets, Lemma <a href="/tag/000X" data-tag="000X">3.11.1</a> to turn $X_{affine, {\acute{e}tale}}$ into a site. </p>
</article>